      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile at a constant speed of 4 miles per hour. Here are the steps to find the solution:\n\n1. **Understand the given information:**\n   - The squirrel's speed is 4 miles per hour.\n\n2. **Convert the speed from miles per hour to miles per minute:**\n   - There are 60 minutes in an hour.\n   - Therefore, to convert the speed from miles per hour to miles per minute, we divide by 60.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed in miles per minute} = \\frac{4 \\text{ miles per hour}}{60 \\text{ minutes per hour}} = \\frac{4}{60} \\text{ miles per minute} = \\frac{1}{15} \\text{ miles per minute}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the time required to travel 1 mile:**\n   - Time is calculated by dividing the distance by the speed.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time in minutes} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{\\frac{1}{15} \\text{ miles per minute}} = 1 \\text{ mile} \\times 15 \\text{ minutes per mile} = 15 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the time it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) minutes.",
