      "text": "To determine how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile, we can use the formula for time, which is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} \\]\n\nGiven that the squirrel travels at a constant speed of 4 miles per hour and the distance to be covered is 1 mile, we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{4 \\text{ miles per hour}} \\]\n\nSince the squirrel travels at a constant speed of 4 miles per hour, it will take 1 hour to travel 1 mile. To convert this time into minutes, we use the fact that 1 hour is equal to 60 minutes:\n\n\\[ \\text{Time in minutes} = 1 \\text{ hour} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour} = 60 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTherefore, the time it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{60} \\]",
